Changes prior to Github transition:
[Jun 29 2026] - Henque
  fix: mob asterisk on map now uses weak/equal/strong color coding
    Mob tiles on the minimap were always yellow regardless of power. Now
    nen_power_rating(ch, mob) is called at render time: weak mobs (<=75%
    of player HP) show yellow, equal (75-125%) show blue, strong (>=125%)
    show red — matching the powerlevel command color convention.
    Three separate entries added to the map legend (Mob(weak/equal/strong)).

[Jun 29 2026] - Henque
  feat: fly mechanic visual polish and worldmap diagonal movement
    - Fly trail glyph now renders in gold (bold yellow) instead of dim-cyan on the worldmap.
    - While a player is auto-flying, their asterisk on the worldmap turns gold; the same applies
      to other players seen on your map.
    - On landing (any arrive mode except Leave), the destination room and all adjacent rooms now
      receive a bolt-of-energy visual: "A bolt of energy descends from the sky near <player>!" in
      the landing room; adjacent rooms get a directional shout giving the compass direction of the
      impact (e.g. "A bolt of energy strikes the ground to the north!").
    - FLY_ARRIVE_PLAYER (Accompany, Magnetic Force): actor now arrives immediately when neither the
      actor nor the destination is on the worldmap, fixing a hang where event_autoflight would loop
      forever trying to walk from a city room toward another city room.
    - flight_direction() now returns diagonal directions (NORTHEAST/NORTHWEST/SOUTHEAST/SOUTHWEST)
      when the destination requires movement on both axes at similar magnitude, enabling diagonal
      auto-flight paths on the worldmap.
    - Diagonal worldmap movement (nw, ne, se, sw commands) now works: virtual diagonal exits for
      all 65536 worldmap rooms are synthesized at boot time in create_worldmap_diagonal_exits()
      (act.movement.c), eliminating the need to add them to 1000.wld. The function logs the count
      of exits created to the boot log.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  fix: transport spell card triggers — replace %ofly% literal with ofly in 10.trg
    Root cause #2: find_replacement() in dg_variables.c (line 316-347) only translates a hardcoded
    whitelist of DG command keywords to their m/o/w-prefixed forms (%send%->osend, %force%->oforce,
    etc.). %ofly% was not in the whitelist, so var_subst resolved it to an empty string. The actor
    UID landed at the start of the line, giving obj_command_interpreter a string like "}6 player
    Nigg group" with no command name -- logging "Unknown object cmd" and silently aborting the flight.
    Fix: write the literal token 'ofly' (no % wrappers) in all 14 ofly calls across triggers
    #1005, #1009, #1013, #1014, #1016, #1017, #1039 in lib/world/trg/10.trg. var_subst copies
    literal text unchanged; ofly %actor% ... resolves to 'ofly }6 ...' which obj_command_interpreter
    correctly dispatches to do_ofly -> start_flight.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  fix: transport spell card command triggers NARG — change 1 c 1 to 1 c 3 (OCMD_EQUIP|OCMD_INVEN)
    Root cause: NARG=1 = OCMD_EQUIP only; cmd_otrig uses IS_SET(narg, type) to gate trigger firing.
    gain with book active reassigns the card from inventory (OCMD_INVEN=2), so IS_SET(1,2)=0 and
    the trigger never fired — do_gain fell through to default "not implemented" on transport vnums.
    Changed 7 transport triggers (#1005, #1009, #1013, #1014, #1016, #1017, #1039) from 1 c 1
    to 1 c 3 so they fire both from equip slot (hold) and inventory.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  fix: transport spell card triggers not blocking do_gain — %arg% parsing and halt semantics
    Root cause: command triggers receive %arg% = full argument after verb (e.g. "acc nigg"),
    so %arg.is_pc% tried to find char named "acc nigg" (fails), trigger fell to city checks,
    those failed too, trigger reached return 0 (allows do_gain) instead of halt.
    Also: dg_owner_purged analysis confirmed return 0 after %purge% %self% is dead code
    (purge causes early exit with ret_val=1 before return 0 is processed).
    Fixes applied to 10.trg:
    - #1005, #1039: %arg.is_pc% -> %arg.cdr.is_pc%; %arg.name% -> %arg.cdr.name%;
      city checks %arg% -> %arg.cdr%; all error-path return 0 -> halt; dead return 0
      after purge removed. Non-gain else kept as return 0 (allow gash, gather, etc.)
    - #1009: same %arg% -> %arg.cdr% for city checks; book-check return 0 -> halt;
      error-path return 0 -> halt; dead return 0 after purge removed.
    - #1013, #1014: book-check return 0 -> halt; dead return 0 after purge removed.
    - #1016: book-check return 0 -> halt; dead return 0 lines after purge removed.
    - #1017: book-check and carried_by return 0 -> halt; dead return 0 after purge
      replaced with break; added else: return 0 for non-gain commands.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  fix: all transport spell cards instant-teleport bug — systematic audit of C-side vs DG trigger
    Root cause: do_gain's switch had cases 1005/1009/1016/1017/1039 calling fly_to_char/fly_to_room
    directly. Since DG triggers didn't halt, both paths ran: trigger started gradual fly, C-side
    immediately teleported. Fixed all 5 cards:
    - Removed cases 1005 (Magnetic Force), 1009 (Return), 1016 (Drift), 1017 (Collision), 1039
      (Accompany) from do_gain switch; DG triggers in trg/10.trg are now sole handlers.
    - Added say messages to #1005 and #1009 triggers (lost when moved to DG).
    - Added halt to #1005, #1009, #1013, #1014 triggers after purge.
    - Added halt after done in #1016 (Drift) and replaced break with halt in #1017 (Collision)
      success path — also fixes #1017's spurious "fails and dissolves" message on success.
    - case 1012 (Relegate) kept: its trigger was not converted to %ofly%, C-side is still owner.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  fix: Accompany card instant-teleport bug — remove C-side case 1039 from do_gain
    The C-side handler in act.item.c was running alongside the DG trigger, calling
    fly_to_char() and bypassing the gradual fly event. Removed case 1039 entirely;
    the DG trigger (trg #1039) now owns all Accompany logic. Added say message and
    halt to the player branch in the trigger.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  feat(p2): transport spell cards — P2 fly mechanic (full implementation)
  Summary of all changes across Tasks 1-7:

  Task 1 (structs.h, constants.c):
  - Added PLR_AUTOFLIGHT (bit 24) to player_bits[] ("AUTOFLIGHT"); used as the
    auto-step lock (look suppression, combat block, manual-move block).
  - Added worldmap grid constants: WORLDMAP_BASE_VNUM 100000, WORLDMAP_GRID 256,
    WORLDMAP_VNUM_TOP, and helpers WORLDMAP_ROW/WORLDMAP_COL/WORLDMAP_VNUM/
    IS_WORLDMAP_ROOM.

  Task 2 (act.movement.c — movement engine):
  - Water gate: added && !AFF_FLAGGED(ch, AFF_FLYING) so flying players cross ocean.
  - Mountain gate: same bypass for mountain terrain.
  - do_simple_move(): look_at_room gated on !PLR_FLAGGED(ch, PLR_AUTOFLIGHT);
    the flight event issues the periodic look instead (every 5 tiles / 1 second).
  - perform_move(): returns 0 with "You're flying..." message if PLR_AUTOFLIGHT set.

  Task 3 (fight.c, mobact.c — combat block):
  - fight.c hit(): early return if attacker or victim has PLR_AUTOFLIGHT.
  - mobact.c mobile_activity(): PLR_AUTOFLIGHT players skipped in both the
    aggressive-mob loop and the memory-mob loop.

  Task 5 (dg_objcmd.c — %ofly% DG command):
  - Added OCMD(do_ofly) registered as "ofly" in the command table.
  - Syntax: %ofly% %actor% city <name> | player <name> | leave | start | room <vnum>
    with optional trailing "group" flag for Accompany.
  - NOHASSLE check: rejects player-mode targets with PRF_NOHASSLE set.

  Task 7 (lib/world/obj/10.obj, lib/world/trg/10.trg — world file wiring):
  - 10.obj: added missing T lines for cards 1005, 1009, 1016, 1017, 1039 (cards
    1013 and 1014 already had T lines). Written in WSL Python binary mode to
    preserve ANSI color bytes.
  - 10.trg: converted all 7 transport card triggers from %teleport%+wait+look to
    %ofly%+%purge% patterns; preserved all gating (is_book, shield_faith,
    visited/met checks, random selection loops). Fixed missing break after %ofly%
    in Collision (#1017) while loop.

[Jun 26 2026] - Henque
  fix(p2): clear PLR_AUTOFLIGHT and AFF_FLYING on player save/load (Task 6)
  - players.c save_char(): snapshot and clear both flags before writing the player
    file; restore them after fclose so a live mid-session save doesn't disrupt an
    actively-flying player. File on disk never carries auto-flight state.
  - players.c load_char(): clear both flags after affect_total() so any stale
    persisted state is stripped before the character enters the world.

