[Jun 25 2026] - Henque
  refine: mountain/hills placement driven by a hand-marked biome mask
  - tools/extract_biome_mask.py (new): reads the marked sample
    (Greed_Island_Map_29_hillvsmountainsample.png; mountains circled red, hills
    purple), fills each circle's interior and downsamples to tools/biome_mask.txt
    (256x256 of M/H/.).
  - tools/biome_mask.txt (new): the generated location authority for high terrain.
  - img_to_map.py: brown terrain becomes mountain/hills ONLY inside the marked
    circles (mountain by default, hills in the purple regions); brown outside any
    circle reverts to field. Enclosed field/forest holes inside a region are filled
    so ranges read as solid clusters with no field speckle in the middle (only
    forest may stay dispersed). Color-only brown denoise is now the fallback used
    only when the mask file is absent.
  - Net effect: mountains are solid clusters in their real locations across the map;
    hills are rare (the two central-south spots); the central-south "mouth" reads as
    hills above / mountain below, as separate biomes.
  - Regenerated greed_island.txt and zone 1000 (1000.wld/1000.zon).
[Jun 25 2026] - Henque
  refine: img_to_map coastal cleanup pass
  - Interior "beach" patches (no ocean/water within 3 tiles) revert to field --
    removes bright dry clearings that were mis-read as beach inland.
  - Real beaches get holes filled: field/forest tiles surrounded by beach become
    beach, so shorelines read as solid sand instead of speckled.
  - Detached islets (land components below 30 tiles, off the main island) are
    dropped to ocean.
  - 1-tile coastal spikes/threads are eroded (a land tile with <=1 land neighbour
    of 4 becomes ocean), removing needless peninsulas; the main island is preserved.
  - Regenerated greed_island.txt and zone 1000 (1000.wld/1000.zon).
[Jun 25 2026] - Henque
  refine: img_to_map terrain classification recalibrated from on-map samples
  - Brightness V (not R-G) now separates hills (light/rust, V>0.60) from mountain
    (dark ridge shadows). Fixes the central "mouth" landmark: light upper lip = hills,
    dark lower lip = mountain (was all mountain before).
  - Weak/coastal browns (R-G <= 15) now fall through to field instead of hills/mountain.
  - Forest is now conservative: only blocks with a clear fraction of dark canopy-shadow
    pixels become forest; everything else defaults to field (field/forest are nearly
    identical in average color in this art). Bias toward field, per design.
  - Spatial denoise: small isolated brown/forest clusters are flipped to field.
  - Roads are no longer auto-generated (cities/roads will be placed by hand later);
    former road pixels become field. Engine 'r'/SECT_CITY mapping retained for manual use.
  - Regenerated lib/world/map/greed_island.txt and zone 1000 (1000.wld/1000.zon).
